# Rendered output is a build artifact — regenerate with `npm run render:reel`.
# catalog.json describes whatever that machine happens to have rendered, so it
# is per-machine too. The directory itself is kept so out/ exists on a clone.
out/*
!out/.gitkeep

# Captures are NOT committed by default.
#
# This repo is PUBLIC, and these are screenshots of a real app carrying seeded
# demo data — the kind of thing that put a real address into the inbox capture
# set. They are also regenerable: `npm run collect`. If a curated capture set
# should ship (marketing/social-assets/ does that), un-ignore it deliberately
# rather than by accident.
public/screens/*
!public/screens/.gitkeep

# src/screens/manifest.json IS committed on purpose: available.ts imports it at
# build time, and without it the placeholder fallback cannot resolve.

node_modules/

# Pulled off the phone by scripts/pull-iphone.ps1. Raw camera-roll media -
# personal by default, and this repo is PUBLIC. Nothing here is ever committed;
# move a vetted capture into public/screens/ deliberately.
ingest/
